  {
   "id": "n-sino",
   "title": "Sino-Korean numbers",
   "rule": "Two number systems. Sino-Korean (일, 이, 삼…) is for money, minutes, dates, phone numbers and anything measured. Bigger numbers are built from the digits: 11 = 십일 (10 + 1), 20 = 이십 (2 × 10). No 일 before 십, 백, 천 or 만: 10 = 십, 100 = 백, 1,000 = 천, 10,000 = 만. Zero is 영, or 공 in phone numbers.",
